#ROOM
Vnum     16000
Name     The Temple Entrance Plaza~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The grand entrance plaza of the Jedi Temple stretches before you,
its pale stone warm in the light. Five spires rise overhead, the
tallest reaching into the sky at the centre. Jedi of all ranks move
purposefully across the plaza — Knights returning from missions,
Padawans in pairs deep in conversation, Masters in quiet reflection.
The atmosphere is one of disciplined serenity. The main temple doors
lie to the north and the approach path leads south.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16002
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16003
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16004
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 2 16000
Reset M 0 16006 2 16000
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16001
Name     The Great Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Great Hall of the Jedi Temple soars overhead in vaulted stone and
pale crystal light. Banners bearing the symbol of the Jedi Order line
the walls from floor to ceiling. At the far end a great mosaic depicts
the founding of the Order in the days of the Republic's earliest
years. Jedi move through this space with unhurried purpose. Corridors
lead east and west and stairs ascend to the north. The entrance plaza
lies to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16000
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16006
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16007
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 2 16001
Reset M 0 16006 1 16001
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16002
Name     The Outer Approach~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A broad processional avenue leads toward the Temple from the south.
Tall trees line the path, their canopies meeting overhead to form a
natural arcade. The path is worn smooth by millennia of feet. Students
and Masters alike walk this route each day and the sense of continuity
is palpable. The Temple entrance plaza lies to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16000
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16002
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16003
Name     The Eastern Garden~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A formal garden occupies the eastern grounds of the Temple complex.
Reflecting pools mirror the spires above and flowering plants native
to a dozen worlds grow in carefully tended beds. Jedi come here to
meditate between duties. The sound of water and the scent of unfamiliar
blossoms create a space that seems deliberately set apart from the
rest of the galaxy. The entrance plaza is to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16000
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16008
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16003
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16004
Name     The Western Garden~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The western gardens are older and less formal than those to the east,
their paths winding between ancient trees whose trunks are wider than
a speeder. Stone benches are placed at intervals and many bear
inscriptions — names of Jedi lost in service to the Order over the
centuries. The weight of that history makes the garden a place of
quiet reverence. The plaza lies to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16000
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16009
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16004
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16005
Name     The Hall of Knighthood~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Hall of Knighthood is where Padawans undergo the Trials and emerge
as Knights. The room is circular with a domed ceiling through which
light filters in shifting patterns. The floor is bare stone worn
smooth by generations of ceremony. Portraits of celebrated Knights
line the curved walls — Ki-Adi-Mundi, Aayla Secura, Depa Billaba,
Kanan Jarrus, and many others. The Great Hall lies to the south and
a corridor leads north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16010
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16011
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 2 16005
Reset M 0 16001 1 16005
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16006
Name     The Eastern Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A long corridor lined with alcoves, each containing a sculpture or
artefact from a significant moment in Jedi history. Informational
plaques in multiple languages accompany each piece. The corridor
connects the Great Hall to the eastern wings of the Temple. Students
often walk slowly here, reading and absorbing the history around them.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16014
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16006
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16007
Name     The Western Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The western corridor of the Great Hall leads toward the Temple's
administrative and residential wings. Notice boards mounted at
intervals carry mission briefings, meditation schedules, and
announcements from the Council. The corridor is busy with Jedi
moving between assignments.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16016
