#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16009
Name     The Memorial Garden~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The memorial garden is the most solemn space in the Temple grounds.
A central monument lists the names of Jedi who gave their lives in
service to the Order and to the Republic. The names number in the
thousands, accumulated over centuries. Fresh flowers are placed here
daily by members of the Order. The western garden leads south and
a path continues north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16004
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16018
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16009
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16010
Name     The Approaches to the High Council Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A formal antechamber before the High Council Chamber, its walls lined
with the names of every Grand Master who has served the Order. The
floor is inlaid with the symbol of the Jedi Order in white and gold
stone. Seating for those awaiting audience with the Council lines the
walls. The atmosphere here is one of controlled gravity. The Hall of
Knighthood lies to the south and the Council Chamber door is to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16019
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16010
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16011
Name     The Hall of Records~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Hall of Records maintains the official chronicle of the Jedi Order —
every mission, every promotion, every loss recorded in meticulous detail.
Archive terminals line one wall and physical records in sealed containers
fill the other. A Jedi archivist manages the retrieval of records for
those with proper authorisation.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16020
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16011
Reset O 0 16004 1 16011
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16012
Name     The Padawan Study Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A large open study hall where Padawans complete their academic work
between training sessions. Long tables are covered in datapads and
physical texts, and the sound of quiet study fills the room. Tutors
circulate, available to answer questions. The walls display rotating
educational projections covering history, science, philosophy, and
the nature of the Force.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16021
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 3 16012
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16013
Name     The Jedi Archives — Main Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Jedi Archives are among the most awe-inspiring spaces in the
galaxy. The main hall extends further than seems architecturally
possible, its shelves rising to heights that require grav-lifts to
reach. Millions of holocrons, datachips, manuscripts, and artefacts
are catalogued and stored here in perfect order. Blue-white light
filters through tall narrow windows and the air carries the particular
smell of very old knowledge.

Jedi Archivist Jocasta Nu moves quietly between the shelves, and the
hush of the Archives feels like a living thing — the accumulated
silence of a million years of careful preservation. The eastern
corridor connects to the south and deeper sections lie ahead.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16006
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16022
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16023
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16024
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16013
Reset O 0 16000 1 16013
Reset O 0 16004 1 16013
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16014
Name     The Map Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A circular room whose walls and ceiling display a continuously updated
holographic map of the known galaxy. Planet systems are marked with
blue light and hyperspace lanes trace silver threads between them.
Mission markers indicate where Jedi are currently deployed. The room
is used for mission briefings and strategic planning. It gives the
impression of the galaxy as a single comprehensible system, which
is both reassuring and humbling.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16006
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16014
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16015
Name     The Mission Assignment Office~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The practical heart of the Temple's administrative operation, the
Mission Assignment Office processes requests for Jedi assistance
from across the Republic. Organised chaos prevails — datapads
everywhere, communications incoming continuously, and a small staff
of dedicated Masters and Knights managing the flow. The western
corridor connects to the south.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16007
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16025
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16015
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16016
Name     The Healers' Waiting Area~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The antechamber to the Jedi Healing Ward, this comfortable waiting
area is designed to put the unwell at ease. Soft lighting, warm
colours, and the gentle sound of water from a small indoor fountain
create a restorative atmosphere. Several Padawans with training
injuries wait quietly. The western corridor is to the east and the
healing ward is to the north.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16007
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16026
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16016
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16017
Name     The High Meditation Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The highest meditation chamber in the Temple, accessible from the
eastern terrace. A domed ceiling of transparisteel gives an unobstructed
view of the sky above. The room is entirely bare except for circular
meditation mats arranged on the floor in a pattern that maximises
the space between practitioners. The Force feels exceptionally clear
here, as though the altitude and the silence thin whatever separates
the practitioner from the living Force.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16008
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16001 1 16017
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16018
Name     The Garden of a Thousand Lights~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     Beyond the memorial garden lies this extraordinary space — a garden
planted over centuries with bioluminescent flora from across the galaxy.
At night the effect is spectacular, the plants glowing in blues, greens,
and soft golds. Even in daylight the garden has an otherworldly quality.
Master Qui-Gon Jinn has been known to sit here for hours in commune with
the living Force.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16009
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16027
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16003 1 16018
Reset M 0 16006 1 16018
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16019
Name     The High Council Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The High Council Chamber occupies the pinnacle of the Temple's tallest
spire. Twelve seats are arranged in a circle, each one the seat of a
Master of the High Council. The floor is transparent and the view
extends across the entire city below. The ceiling is similarly open
to the sky above.

The chair of Grand Master Yoda sits slightly elevated from the rest.
The chamber carries the weight of a thousand years of decisions made
here — good decisions and flawed ones alike. The antechamber lies below.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16010
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16000 1 16019
Reset M 0 16002 1 16019
Reset M 0 16001 1 16019
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16020
Name     The Restricted Archives~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A section of the Archives accessible only to Masters and those with
specific Council authorisation. The restricted collection contains
records of Sith artefacts, dark side techniques catalogued for
research purposes, sensitive mission records, and knowledge deemed
too dangerous for general access. Jocasta Nu guards the entrance
with impeccable seriousness.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16011
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16020
Reset O 0 16000 1 16020
Reset O 0 16004 1 16020
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16021
Name     The Youngling Training Area~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The training area for the youngest Temple students — the Younglings who
have not yet been selected as Padawans. Small mats and scaled-down
training equipment fill the space. The walls are decorated with simple
illustrations of famous Jedi and explanations of the Code. The sound
of children learning to meditate, concentrate, and take their first
tentative steps with the Force fills the room with an energy that is
both energetic and surprisingly moving.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16012
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16028
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 3 16021
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16022
Name     The Holocron Vault~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A vault within the Archives dedicated entirely to the storage of
Jedi holocrons — thousands of them, each containing the recorded
knowledge and personality of a Jedi Master. Pyramid-shaped and cube-
shaped, glowing blue or gold, they fill shelf after shelf in precise
arrangement. The combined presence of so many preserved Force-sensitive
minds gives the room a particular quality — like standing in the
presence of an immense, patient, multivocal intelligence.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16029
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16022
Reset O 0 16000 1 16022
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16023
Name     The Historical Wing~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The historical wing of the Archives covers the first ten thousand years
of the Jedi Order. Records of the Hundred Year Darkness, the Great
Hyperspace War, the Mandalorian Wars, and the New Sith Wars are all
here in extraordinary detail. The oldest documents are sealed in
preservation containers and available only through high-resolution
holographic reproductions.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16013
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 16004 1 16023
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16024
Name     The Science and Navigation Wing~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The scientific and navigational collection covers astronomy,
xenobiology, medicine, physics, and every navigational chart the
Order has ever compiled. It is here that Jedi researchers have
made some of their most significant contributions to galactic
knowledge. The terminals in this wing are among the most advanced
in the Temple and are in constant use.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16013
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16024
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16025
Name     The Dispatch Centre~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The operational hub of the Temple's mission operations, the Dispatch
Centre runs on a constant stream of incoming intelligence, mission
updates, and communication from Jedi in the field. Holographic
displays cover every wall and the room is never quiet. Jedi Knights
and Masters rotate through on duty shifts, ensuring the Order's
response capacity never sleeps.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16015
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16030
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 2 16025
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16026
Name     The Healing Ward~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Jedi Healing Ward combines medical technology with Force-assisted
recovery techniques. Private treatment areas line the walls and a
central space is available for more intensive care. Jedi Healers
move between patients with calm efficiency. The atmosphere is one
of disciplined compassion. Several Jedi Masters have noted that
recovery here is remarkably swift — a combination of skill and the
healing properties of the Force.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16016
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16026
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16027
Name     The Contemplation Path~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A winding path through the northern gardens used specifically for
walking meditation. Unlike seated meditation, the walking form
encourages integration of awareness with movement. Master Yoda
and Master Qui-Gon Jinn have both been known to walk this path
daily. Smooth stones are set at intervals and the path curves through
stands of carefully cultivated trees from Kashyyyk and Felucia.
The garden of lights lies south and the path continues north.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16018
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16031
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16027
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16028
Name     The Youngling Dormitory~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Simple, clean, and warmly lit, the Youngling dormitory houses the
Temple's youngest students in small but comfortable quarters. Each
young Force-sensitive has a bunk, a personal storage unit, and a
small window. The walls are decorated with the students' own artwork
alongside educational displays. The sound of sleeping children and
the occasional murmur of a nightmare — quickly soothed by a watching
Jedi — fills the night hours.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16021
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16028
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16029
Name     The Master's Reading Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A quiet room within the Archives reserved for senior Masters engaged
in deep research. Individual study alcoves line the walls, each with
full archive access. The Jedi Code is inscribed in large text above
the entrance: There is no emotion, there is peace. There is no
ignorance, there is knowledge. There is no passion, there is serenity.
There is no chaos, there is harmony. There is no death, there is
the Force. Master Obi-Wan Kenobi can sometimes be found here.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16022
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16001 1 16029
Reset O 0 16004 1 16029
Reset O 0 16000 1 16029
Reset O 0 16009 1 16029
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16030
Name     The Strategic Operations Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A secure room within the Dispatch Centre used for sensitive mission
planning. Access is restricted to Masters and Knights with relevant
clearance. Holographic displays show real-time intelligence from
across the Republic. Master Mace Windu chairs the regular briefings
held in this room with the brisk efficiency he brings to all things.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16025
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16002 1 16030
Reset M 0 16005 1 16030
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16031
Name     The Northern Grounds~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The northern grounds of the Temple complex are the most open area
within the walls — a broad expanse of carefully maintained grass
used for outdoor training, group meditation, and ceremonial gatherings.
The five spires of the Temple frame the view to the south. To the
north the outer wall of the complex is visible. Paths lead toward
the training facilities.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16027
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16032
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16033
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16034
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16031
Reset M 0 16005 1 16031
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16032
Name     The Approach to the Training Halls~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A broad corridor leading from the northern grounds into the Temple's
training complex. The walls here are covered in diagrams of lightsaber
forms — Shii-Cho, Makashi, Soresu, Ataru, Shien, Niman, and Juyo
illustrated in precise detail with annotations in multiple languages.
Students study these as they walk, and it is not unusual to see a
Padawan pause mid-stride to examine a particular stance. The northern
grounds lie south and the training halls are ahead.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16031
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16035
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16036
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16037
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16032
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16033
Name     The Armoury~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Temple armoury maintains the Order's inventory of training
equipment, ceremonial items, and mission gear. Racks of training
lightsabers — low-powered versions for sparring — line one wall.
Equipment for stealth, climbing, survival, and other mission needs
fills the rest of the space. An armourer Jedi Knight manages the
inventory with characteristic precision.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16031
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16033
Reset O 0 16001 1 16033
Reset O 0 16010 1 16033
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16034
Name     The Equipment Store~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The equipment store supplies ongoing needs of Temple residents —
robes, boots, belts, medpacs, comlinks, and the various practical
items required for daily life in the Order. Everything is organised
with Jedi thoroughness. The store also carries components for
lightsaber construction, a constant area of interest for Padawans
approaching the trials.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16031
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 16002 1 16034
Reset O 0 16003 1 16034
Reset O 0 16011 1 16034
Reset O 0 16012 1 16034
Reset O 0 16013 1 16034
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16035
Name     The Primary Training Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The primary training hall is a large open space with high ceilings
that allow for aerial combat training. The floor is a specialised
material that reduces impact from falls without being so soft as
to remove the lesson. Training equipment is stored along the walls
and the space can be configured in multiple ways.

Training remotes hover at various heights throughout the room,
their sensors tracking all movement, ready to engage any student
who activates them. Master Ahsoka Tano oversees training sessions
here with the hands-on engagement of someone who learned to fight
young and values practical experience above theory.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16032
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16038
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16039
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16040
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16004 1 16035
Reset M 0 16007 5 16035
Reset O 0 16005 1 16035
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16036
Name     The Theory Classroom~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A classroom used for the academic side of Jedi training — Force theory,
the history of the Order, ethics, law, diplomacy, and the study of
species and cultures encountered in the field. Rows of desks face a
teaching station equipped with holographic projection. The walls
display rotating quotations from Jedi Masters across history,
including Obi-Wan Kenobi, Luminara Unduli, and Plo Koon.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16032
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 3 16036
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16037
Name     The Meditation Instruction Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A dedicated room for the teaching and practice of Jedi meditation
techniques. The lighting can be adjusted from full illumination to
near-complete darkness. Sound dampening built into the walls creates
a silence deeper than most rooms can achieve. Meditation mats are
arranged in a circle and a central raised platform allows an
instructor to guide sessions. Master Yoda teaches here on occasion,
and the sessions are attended by students at every level.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16032
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16000 1 16037
Reset M 0 16006 2 16037
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16038
Name     The Advanced Combat Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The advanced combat hall is reserved for Knights and Masters engaged
in serious sparring. The room is significantly larger than the
primary hall and equipped with more sophisticated training remotes
capable of coordinated attacks. The walls are scarred from years of
lightsaber practice and the floor shows the marks of countless bouts.

Master Mace Windu has been known to run sessions here in the
Vaapad form, though he is careful to find suitable partners — the
form is dangerous in untrained hands.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16035
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16041
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 3 16038
Reset M 0 16007 3 16038
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16039
Name     The Force Training Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A specialised room for training Force abilities — telekinesis,
Force sense, Force push and pull, mind techniques, and the subtler
applications of the living Force. Suspended objects at various
heights serve as targets and props. Sensors measure the strength
and precision of Force applications and provide real-time feedback.

Master Plo Koon has added several training modules to this
room based on his own extensive experience with telekinetic
combat applications developed over decades of active service.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16035
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16009 1 16039
Reset M 0 16006 2 16039
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16040
Name     The Lightsaber Construction Workshop~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Every Jedi must construct their own lightsaber — it is a rite of
passage requiring patience, Force attunement, and technical skill.
This workshop provides the tools and environment for that process.
Workbenches with precision tools, a selection of components, and
a temperature-controlled kyber crystal storage unit fill the room.

The walls display detailed schematics for a dozen lightsaber
configurations alongside notes from Masters who have overseen
thousands of constructions. Among the most annotated is a set
of notes in a familiar hand — Obi-Wan Kenobi's, covering
every common mistake a Padawan can make.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16035
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16001 1 16040
Reset O 0 16001 1 16040
Reset O 0 16006 1 16040
Reset O 0 16008 1 16040
Reset O 0 16013 1 16040
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16041
Name     The Obstacle Course~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     An elaborate obstacle course used for agility, balance, and focus
training. Moving platforms, suspended beams, vertical climbing walls,
and Force-navigation puzzles make up a constantly reconfigurable
challenge. Students time their runs and the records are posted on
a board near the entrance.

Ahsoka Tano holds several course records and will cheerfully tell
anyone who asks. No one has come close to breaking them.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16038
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16042
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16041
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16042
Name     The Outdoor Training Grounds~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     Open-air training grounds at the northern end of the Temple complex.
Used for exercises that benefit from natural conditions — variable
light, wind, uneven terrain. Several courses are set up here at any
given time, including a distance-running track that circles the entire
compound. Morning training sessions here are a Temple tradition going
back centuries, and sunrise over the city from this position is
genuinely spectacular.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16041
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16043
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16044
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 3 16042
Reset M 0 16005 1 16042
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16043
Name     The Eastern Residential Wing — Entrance~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The entrance to the eastern residential wing where Jedi Knights
and visiting Masters are quartered. The corridor is quieter than
the training areas, maintained at a lower level of activity to
allow for rest and personal study. Each resident has private
quarters with a workspace, meditation space, and basic amenities.
The outdoor grounds lie to the west.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16042
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16045
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16046
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 2 16043
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16044
Name     The Western Residential Wing — Entrance~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The entrance to the western residential wing, which houses Padawans
and their Masters in paired quarters designed to facilitate the
Master-Padawan relationship. The layout puts each apprentice
adjacent to their teacher, a practical recognition that the
Jedi apprenticeship never really ends at the training hall door.
The outdoor grounds lie to the east.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16042
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16047
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16044
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16045
Name     Obi-Wan Kenobi's Quarters~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The personal quarters of Master Obi-Wan Kenobi are characteristically
understated — a meditation mat, a modest desk covered in mission
reports and historical texts, a simple bunk, and a rack for his
robes. A small collection of items on a shelf tells a quiet story:
a hologram of Qui-Gon Jinn, a worn copy of the Jedi Code, and a
datapad with a half-written letter to a former Padawan. The room
is orderly, inhabited, and unmistakably his.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16043
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16001 1 16045
Reset O 0 16004 1 16045
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16046
Name     The Knight's Common Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A common room shared by the Knights quartered in the eastern wing.
Comfortable seating, a kitchen unit, and a recreational terminal
make it a place where Jedi genuinely relax — or as close to it as
their training permits. Mission stories are exchanged here, strategies
debated, and the occasional game of dejarik played with a competitiveness
that would surprise those who imagine Jedi as uniformly serene.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16043
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 2 16046
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16047
Name     The Padawan Common Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Padawan common room is livelier than its Knight equivalent. Young
Jedi in various stages of training gather here between sessions to
compare notes, help each other study, debate the finer points of
the Force, and occasionally just be young people in a galaxy that
asks a great deal of them. The walls are covered in a mix of
training schedules, philosophical quotations, and student artwork.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16044
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16048
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 3 16047
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16048
Name     Master Yoda's Chambers~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Grand Master Yoda's personal chambers are strikingly simple for one
of the most powerful beings in the galaxy. A sleeping space scaled
to his small frame, a meditation area, and a modest collection of
objects accumulated over nine centuries. A small pot of warming
broth sits perpetually on a heating element. Several gimer sticks
lean against one wall.

The most striking feature is a collection of small handwritten notes
pinned around the doorframe — observations, reminders, questions
without answers. Nine hundred years of wondering, reduced to scraps
of paper. The chambers radiate a profound and unassuming peace.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16047
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16000 1 16048
Reset O 0 16000 1 16048
Reset O 0 16009 1 16048
Reset O 0 16007 1 16048
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16049
Name     The Temple Refectory~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Temple refectory serves three meals daily to the entire Temple
population. Long communal tables fill the space and the kitchen
staff — both Jedi and civilian — maintain a standard that is
nourishing if not extravagant. Jedi tradition holds that meals
should be taken in company and conversation, and the refectory
at mealtimes is one of the more genuinely social spaces in
the Temple. It connects to the residential wings and the main corridors.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16044
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16043
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16042
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16049
Reset M 0 16005 1 16049
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16050
Name     The Lower Archive Vaults~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Below the main Archive level, accessible by lift, the lower vaults
contain the most ancient and most sensitive items in the Jedi
collection. The temperature and humidity are precisely controlled.
Some of the items here predate the Republic itself. Others were
seized from Sith collections over centuries and are kept here
under study. The presence of so much accumulated history creates
a weight in the Force that is almost tangible.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    16013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16051
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16050
Reset O 0 16000 1 16050
Reset O 0 16004 1 16050
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16051
Name     The Artefact Repository~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The artefact repository stores physical objects of historical or
Force significance — ancient weapons, ceremonial items, recovered
Sith relics under containment, and personal effects of notable
Jedi preserved for historical record. Each item is catalogued and
contained according to its specific properties. Some containers
have additional Force-imbued seals placed by senior Masters.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16050
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16051
Reset O 0 16004 1 16051
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16052
Name     The Spire Observation Deck~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The observation deck of the Temple's central spire, at the very
summit. The view from here encompasses the entire city stretching
to every horizon, with the Republic's infrastructure spread below
like a living map. At night the city lights make the view extraordinary.

Jedi Masters come here for perspective — both literally and
figuratively. The isolation of the height and the view of so much
that the Order serves and protects makes it a powerful place for
clarity of purpose.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    16019
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16002 1 16052
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16053
Name     The Jedi Code Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A small dedicated chamber near the Hall of Knighthood where the Jedi
Code is inscribed in full in a hundred languages on every surface.
Initiates are brought here early in their training and Knights
return before taking the Trials. The room is available to all
at all hours and is rarely empty. The Code in Aurebesh script
dominates the ceiling — large enough to read while lying on
the meditation mat below.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16005
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16053
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16054
Name     The Communications Centre~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Temple's communications hub handles all incoming and outgoing
contact with Jedi in the field, Republic officials, and planetary
governments. Encrypted channels to every significant location in
the Republic run through this centre. The operator Jedi maintain
focus and composure regardless of the nature of the communications
passing through their stations.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16025
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 2 16054
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16055
Name     The Quartermaster's Office~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The practical logistics of Temple life are managed from this office —
supply requisitions, equipment maintenance schedules, construction
and repair requests, and the thousand administrative details that
keep a large complex functioning. The Jedi Knight who manages this
office has a gift for organisation that they apply with the same
quiet professionalism as any other aspect of their service.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16015
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16055
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16056
Name     The Temple Council Anteroom~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A formal waiting area outside the High Council Chamber proper, used
when the Council meets in closed session. The room is furnished
with dignified simplicity and the weight of decisions pending review
by the twelve Masters can be felt in the quiet. Those waiting here
learn patience in an environment specifically designed to encourage it.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16019
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16010
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16056
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16057
Name     The Diplomatic Reception Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     When Republic officials, planetary delegations, or other formal visitors
attend the Temple, they are received in this chamber. The room is
notably more formal than the rest of the Temple — elegant furnishings,
careful lighting, and a layout designed to impress without intimidating.
The Order's diplomatic work is as important as its peacekeeping and
this space reflects that fact.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16001 1 16057
Reset M 0 16005 1 16057
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16058
Name     The Temple Library Reading Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A reading room adjacent to the main Archives, less imposing than the
great hall of the Archives but with full access to the collection
via terminals. Individual reading alcoves provide privacy. The room
is used by both Jedi and approved outside researchers. The quiet here
has been described by multiple visitors as the most peaceful they
have ever experienced.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16024
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16058
Reset M 0 16008 1 16058
Reset O 0 16004 1 16058
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16059
Name     The Illuminated Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A long corridor running the length of the Archives' eastern face,
its walls made of translucent stone that glows with a soft blue light
absorbed from the kyber crystal deposits in the Temple's foundations.
The effect is beautiful and has a subtle calming property confirmed
by multiple studies. It connects the Archive wings to the training
approach.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16006
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16059
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16060
Name     The Initiate Assessment Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Where new Force-sensitives are assessed upon arriving at the Temple.
The primary instrument is a blood sample analysis for midi-chlorian
count, supplemented by practical observation exercises. The room is
deliberately non-threatening in design — comfortable and warm, with
a gentle light and toys for the youngest arrivals. The experience
of being assessed here is the first step for most Jedi.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16021
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16001 1 16060
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16061
Name     The Lightsaber Forms Study~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A dedicated study room for the theoretical and holographic study of
lightsaber combat forms. Life-size holographic recordings of Masters
demonstrating each form can be called up and studied from any angle
at any speed. The seven classical forms — Shii-Cho, Makashi, Soresu,
Ataru, Shien, Niman, and Juyo — and their variants are all catalogued.
Annotations from Master Cin Drallig, the Temple's chief swordsmanship
instructor, accompany each recording.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16035
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16061
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16062
Name     The Sparring Ring~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A circular sparring ring with clear sightlines from all angles, used
for supervised combat training. The ring is bounded by a low energy
barrier that stops combatants from accidentally leaving the space but
does not interfere with the fight itself. Benches for observation
ring the outside. Scheduled sparring sessions run most of the day
and informal matches are permitted in off-hours.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16038
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16035
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 2 16062
Reset M 0 16007 2 16062
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16063
Name     The Balance Training Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A room dedicated to the physical balance training that underpins
lightsaber technique. Narrow beams at various heights, balance boards,
and suspended platforms are arranged throughout. Training remotes
set to low-intensity operation add a layer of challenge for advanced
students. Master Yoda insists that physical balance and mental balance
are the same thing approached from different directions.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16038
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16007 3 16063
Reset M 0 16006 2 16063
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16064
Name     The Wisdom Corridor~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A corridor connecting the Hall of Knighthood to the residential wings,
its walls lined with handwritten texts from Jedi Masters across
history. Unlike the formal inscriptions elsewhere in the Temple,
these are reproductions of informal writings — journal entries,
letters, notes to students, observations made in the field. The
humanity and variety of Jedi experience expressed here makes this
one of the most visited spaces in the Temple.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16047
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16043
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16064
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16065
Name     The Jedi Temple Hangar~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Temple hangar maintains a modest fleet of transport vessels for
Jedi use. Several Jedi Starfighters — the compact single-seat fighters
used for rapid deployment — rest in maintenance bays alongside a
larger transport shuttle. Astromech droids move between the ships,
running diagnostics and carrying out routine maintenance. The bay
connects to the northern grounds.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16031
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16065
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16066
Name     The Kyber Crystal Storage~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Adjacent to the lightsaber construction workshop, a temperature and
pressure-controlled storage space for kyber crystals. The crystals
are the heart of every lightsaber and obtaining one through the
traditional pilgrimage to Ilum is a Padawan rite of passage. The
storage here holds reserve crystals, study specimens, and crystals
recovered from destroyed lightsabers for examination.

The crystals hum faintly in their storage cells and the combined
effect is a sound at the very edge of hearing that practitioners
describe as comforting.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16040
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 16001 1 16066
Reset O 0 16006 1 16066
Reset O 0 16008 1 16066
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16067
Name     The Temple Archives — Cataloguing Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The working space where new acquisitions to the Archives are
processed — catalogued, described, dated, and assigned to their
appropriate location. The work is painstaking and requires both
scholarly knowledge and Force sensitivity to properly assess
certain items. Jocasta Nu maintains that this room is the most
important in the Archives, since an uncatalogued item is a lost
item regardless of its significance.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16013
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16067
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16068
Name     The Temple Inner Courtyard~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     An enclosed courtyard at the heart of the Temple complex, accessible
from several interior corridors. A single massive tree grows here,
its trunk wider than three people can encircle, its age unknown.
Jedi lore holds that the tree was already ancient when the Temple
was built around it, and that it is sensitive to the Force in ways
that science has confirmed but not explained. Sitting beneath it
is said to be profoundly clarifying.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16005
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16013
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16035
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16000 1 16068
Reset M 0 16006 2 16068
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16069
Name     The Chamber of Becoming~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A small private chamber used for the final stage of the Jedi Trials —
the Trial of the Spirit. Here a Jedi faces a deeply personal vision
constructed by the Force itself, confronting fears, attachments, and
the shadow of the dark side within. Masters do not enter with the
student. What happens here is intensely private.

The room is otherwise unremarkable in its appointments, which seems
fitting. The most significant experiences rarely require elaborate
staging.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16010
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16000 1 16069
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16070
Name     The Temple Bell Tower~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A narrow tower containing the Temple bell, rung to mark significant
moments in Temple life — dawn meditation, meals, ceremonies, and
the rare occasions when an emergency requires all Temple residents
to gather. The bell is cast from an alloy that includes kyber
crystal fragments, giving its tone a quality that can be felt
as much as heard by Force-sensitives. From the tower's small
windows the city spreads in every direction.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16071
Name     The Masters' Contemplation Hall~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A hall reserved for Jedi Masters in need of extended private
contemplation. Unlike the meditation rooms available to all members
of the Order, this space is maintained in absolute silence by
sound-dampening technology and additional Force-imbued insulation
applied by senior Masters over generations. Nothing of the outside
world penetrates here. Masters come to this room when decisions
of great weight must be made.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16010
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16003 1 16071
Reset M 0 16000 1 16071
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16072
Name     The Temple Basement — Utility Corridors~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The utilitarian underbelly of the Temple — power conduits, water
systems, climate control units, and the various mechanical systems
that keep a building of this scale functional. Maintenance droids
move through these corridors constantly. The contrast with the
Temple above is total — here everything is functional and
unloved, which gives the basement an oddly honest quality.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    16068
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16073
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16073
Name     The Deep Foundation Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     The deepest accessible point beneath the Temple, where the original
foundations meet the bedrock of the planet. The kyber crystals
embedded in the foundations are largest here, their glow the only
illumination — a shifting blue that gives the chamber an underwater
quality. The hum of their combined resonance is constant and low.

Very few Jedi come here and those who do report that the Force
feels different at this depth — more present, less directed.
As though the crystal-laced bedrock acts as an amplifier for the
living Force in a way that the architects of the Temple understood
and deliberately incorporated.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16072
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16000 1 16073
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16074
Name     The Temple Outpost~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A small outpost at the Temple's outer perimeter, maintained by
rotating duty Jedi Knights. The outpost monitors the approach to
the Temple and provides a first point of contact for visitors.
It is also simply a pleasant place to stand watch — the view of
the Temple entrance plaza from here, framed by the processional
avenue trees, is one that many Jedi remember long after leaving.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16000
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 2 16074
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16075
Name     The Night Watch Post~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A watch post active during the night cycle, when the Temple is
quieter but never entirely still. The Jedi on night watch monitor
the Temple's security systems, handle any communications that come
in during off-hours, and maintain the presence of the Order even
in the deep hours. The night watch is considered a meditative
assignment — long stretches of quiet attention punctuated by
moments of decisive action.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16074
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16075
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16076
Name     The Jedi Temple Archives — Species Reference Wing~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A wing of the Archives dedicated to xenobiology and species
documentation — one of the most extensively used sections by Jedi
preparing for missions to unfamiliar worlds. Tens of thousands of
species are documented here with information on biology, culture,
language, history, and Force sensitivity rates. The collection
is updated continuously as Jedi return from the field.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16023
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16076
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16077
Name     The Diplomatic Records Wing~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Treaties, diplomatic correspondence, records of negotiations mediated
by the Jedi, and the history of the Order's relationship with the
Republic and its predecessors fill this wing of the Archives. It
is the wing that senior Padawans preparing for missions involving
political mediation study most intensively. Master Obi-Wan Kenobi
is said to have nearly lived here as a Padawan.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16024
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 16004 1 16077
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16078
Name     The Force Nexus Meditation Space~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A meditation space built directly over the strongest convergence of
kyber crystal deposits in the Temple's foundations. The Force presence
here is powerful enough to affect even non-sensitives, who report
feeling unusually calm and clear after spending time in the room.
For Force-sensitives the experience is considerably more intense.
Several of the Order's most significant insights have come to Masters
meditating in this room.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    16068
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16000 1 16078
Reset M 0 16009 1 16078
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16079
Name     The Jedi Temple — Roof Garden~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     The roof of the Temple's lower sections has been cultivated into a
garden accessible from several interior stairways. The elevation
provides a remarkable view in all directions and the garden itself
is maintained with the careful attention the Order brings to all
things. Jedi come here for a combination of the view, the fresh
air, and the slight remove from the activity below. Master Ahsoka
Tano has been known to train here at dawn.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16004 1 16079
Reset M 0 16006 1 16079
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16080
Name     The Jedi Council Secondary Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A secondary Council meeting space used for smaller deliberations that
do not require the full High Council. Four or five Masters can meet
here for specific discussions without convening the full Council
in its chamber at the spire's summit. The room is furnished simply
and the lack of formality relative to the High Council Chamber is
intentional — some discussions benefit from it.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16010
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16002 1 16080
Reset M 0 16001 1 16080
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16081
Name     The Temple Infirmary Annex~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     An annex to the main Healing Ward for overflow capacity and for
cases requiring extended recovery. The rooms here are more private
than the main ward and are used for Jedi recovering from serious
injuries or from the particular exhaustion that follows deep Force
work. The quiet is significant and carefully maintained.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16026
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16005 1 16081
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16082
Name     The Temple Archives — Restricted Reading Alcove~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A restricted reading alcove within the Archives where sensitive
documents can be reviewed under supervised conditions. The alcove
is shielded against recording devices and the contents of documents
reviewed here cannot be copied or transmitted. Access requires
authorisation from a Council Master or from Jocasta Nu herself,
who grants it with the particular reluctance of someone who knows
exactly how dangerous knowledge can be.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16020
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16082
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16083
Name     The Temple Commissary~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The Temple commissary supplies consumables, replacement equipment,
and general supplies to Temple residents. It is not a shop in any
commercial sense — items are requisitioned, not purchased — but
the function is similar. The commissary Jedi manages inventory
with meticulous care and has been known to remember exactly what
every Temple resident needs before they arrive to ask for it.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16049
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 16002 1 16083
Reset O 0 16003 1 16083
Reset O 0 16012 1 16083
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16084
Name     The Temple Gardens — Fountain Court~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A courtyard within the formal eastern gardens, built around a
central fountain whose water cascades through a series of tiered
stone basins before collecting in a reflecting pool. The sound
of the water is the only sound in this part of the gardens.
Jedi who seek clarity often find themselves here without quite
remembering the decision to come.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16003
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16084
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16085
Name     The Temple Gardens — Ancient Tree Grove~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A grove of ancient trees within the western gardens, their trunks
marked by centuries. These particular trees were transplanted from
Endor generations ago and carry a faint Force sensitivity that makes
the grove feel inhabited in a way that is difficult to articulate.
Small glowing creatures sometimes emerge from the bark at dusk.
Master Qui-Gon Jinn considers this the finest spot in the Temple.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16004
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16003 1 16085
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16086
Name     The Padawan Examination Room~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Where Padawans undergo formal assessments of their academic and
practical progress. The room contains both a written examination
terminal and a practical demonstration space. The assessments
are rigorous but fair — the Jedi believe that knowing one's
actual level of competence is more valuable than the comfort of
overestimating it.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16012
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16001 1 16086
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16087
Name     The Force History Chamber~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A chamber dedicated to the history of the Force itself — what is
known of its origins, the various traditions that have sought to
understand it, the balance between its aspects, and the ongoing
scholarly debate about its nature. The room contains some of the
most ancient documents in the Archive collection. Reading them
produces more questions than answers, which the Jedi consider
entirely appropriate.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16022
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 16004 1 16087
Reset O 0 16000 1 16087
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16088
Name     The Training Hall Observation Balcony~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A balcony above the primary training hall where Masters and senior
Knights can observe training sessions without participating. It is
also used by students to watch advanced training and by Masters
to watch students who do not know they are being observed — which
reveals considerably more about a Padawan's development than any
formal assessment.
~
#EXIT
Direction down~
ToRoom    16035
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16001 1 16088
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16089
Name     The Meditation Cave~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors dark~
Desc     A natural cave beneath the Temple gardens, accessible through a
concealed entrance in the western garden. Unlike the designed
meditation spaces above, this cave is unchanged from its natural
state. It is cold, dark, and utterly without comfort. Masters
send students here specifically because of that — some experiences
with the Force require the removal of all distraction, including
the distraction of pleasantness.

Master Yoda has meditated here more times than he can count,
which at nine hundred years is saying something.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    16004
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16000 1 16089
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16090
Name     The Temple Archives — Prophecy Collection~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A specific section of the Archives devoted to Jedi prophecy — a
subject treated with a mixture of scholarly interest and philosophical
caution within the Order. The most famous prophecy, concerning the
Chosen One who will bring balance to the Force, is documented here
in seventeen different translations and accompanied by centuries of
interpretive commentary. The commentary is notably inconclusive.
~
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16029
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16008 1 16090
Reset O 0 16004 1 16090
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16091
Name     The Temple — The Thousand Steps~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The great ceremonial staircase descending from the Temple's main
entrance level to the plaza below — one thousand steps of pale
stone worn by the passage of countless generations. Walking the
Thousand Steps is itself considered a meditative practice by
many Jedi. The view from the top is of the processional avenue
stretching south toward the city. The view from the bottom is
of the Temple rising into the sky.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16000
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16002
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 2 16091
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16092
Name     The Temple Archives — Force Cartography Wing~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     Maps of Force nexuses, vergences, and sensitive locations across the
galaxy fill this wing of the Archives. The collection includes charts
of Dagobah, Ilum, Mortis (theoretical), the Cave of Evil on Dagobah,
the World Between Worlds entrance on Lothal, and dozens of other
significant Force locations. The cartography is maintained by a small
team and updated as new locations are identified.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16024
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 16004 1 16092
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16093
Name     The Jedi Temple — The Sunken Courtyard~
Sector   field~
Flags    ~
Desc     A sunken courtyard accessible by steps from the main level, its floor
two metres below the surrounding paths. The sunken design creates
a natural windbreak and a sense of enclosure that makes it feel
more private than any interior room. A small flowering tree at
the centre is the only plant in an otherwise stone space. Jedi
use this courtyard for private conversations and difficult discussions
that benefit from a degree of separation from the Temple's activity.
~
#EXIT
Direction up~
ToRoom    16068
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16001 1 16093
Reset M 0 16006 1 16093
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16094
Name     The Temple Archives — Navigation and Astronomy Wing~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The most technically specialised section of the Archives, housing
star charts, hyperspace route maps, gravitational surveys, and
astronomical data accumulated by the Order over millennia. The
data here has contributed significantly to Republic navigation.
The Jedi's unique ability to detect Force-sensitive navigation
hazards — maelstroms, mass shadows with unusual properties —
has made their astronomical collection particularly valuable.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16024
#ENDEXIT

Reset O 0 16004 1 16094
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16095
Name     The Temple — The Way of Peace~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A corridor connecting the residential wings to the training complex,
its walls inlaid with a continuous relief depicting peaceful scenes —
gardens, conversations, children learning, healers working. It is
a deliberate counterpoint to the combat training it leads toward,
a reminder of what the training is in service of. Most Jedi walk
this corridor without consciously reading the imagery. Most
have absorbed it anyway.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16035
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16044
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16095
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16096
Name     The Temple — The Hall of Service~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A hall dedicated to the memory of Jedi who distinguished themselves
through service — not in combat, which has its own memorials, but
in healing, diplomacy, teaching, and the quiet work that never makes
the history records but without which the galaxy would be measurably
worse. The names and brief accounts here represent thousands of
lives spent in acts whose significance was invisible at the time
and only apparent in retrospect.
~
#EXIT
Direction west~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT

Reset M 0 16006 1 16096
#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16097
Name     The Temple — The Threshold~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     The innermost threshold of the Temple — a simple doorway with no
particular architectural distinction, standing between the active
spaces of the Order and the deepest meditation areas. Tradition
holds that one pauses here to set aside whatever one is carrying
before proceeding, and to acknowledge what one is returning to.
The tradition is observed more often than not.
~
#EXIT
Direction north~
ToRoom    16068
#ENDEXIT
#EXIT
Direction south~
ToRoom    16001
#ENDEXIT

#ENDROOM

#ROOM
Vnum     16098
Name     The Temple — The Room of a Thousand Candles~
Sector   inside~
Flags    indoors~
Desc     A circular room lit entirely by candles — one thousand of them, in
holders of varying heights arranged in concentric circles. The candles
are the first thing Younglings learn to light using the Force and
the last thing Knights extinguish before beginning the Trials. Keeping
all one thousand lit simultaneously is said to be achievable only by
those who have genuinely mastered inner stillness. The room is never
dark and never cold.
~
#EXIT
Direction east~
ToRoom    16069
#ENDEXIT
